# AI Engine — Training & Accuracy Testing Plan

## What We're Building

The existing `detection.py` already uses **YOLOv8n-pose** (a pre-trained model) — we don't retrain the neural network weights (that needs a GPU cluster). Instead, we:

1. **Tune & validate the fall-detection logic** (the aspect-ratio + state-machine thresholds that sit on top of YOLO)
2. **Build a synthetic test suite** that tests accuracy without needing a live camera
3. **Add a benchmark script** that measures real-world performance metrics (FPS, detection rate, fall detection accuracy)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> "Training" here = **threshold calibration** of our fall-detection algorithm (aspect ratio, confirm frames, duration timers). YOLOv8 itself is already trained — we use it as-is.

---

## Open Questions (None — proceeding with implementation)

